        cn: '⭐ 1219-1221 年——我 57 到 59 岁——西征花剌子模（Khwarezmid）。\n\n起因：1218 年我派 450 人商队 + 蒙古使节去花剌子模通商——商队到 Otrar（今哈萨克斯坦境内）——总督 Inalchuq 怀疑商队是间谍——杀了全部 450 人。\n\n我又派使节去抗议——花剌子模沙王 Muhammad II 烧了使节胡须——按草原外交法这是宣战。\n\n1219 年春我率 10-15 万骑兵——翻天山——3 年灭掉 Persia 东部最大国家。\n\n1220 年屠 Bukhara（不花剌，今乌兹别克）——围城后我骑马进城清真寺——把可兰经撕下来扔在马厩地上——城中 3 万守军全杀（Juvayni 1252 数字；21c 学界 Peter Jackson 2017 estimate 在 1-3 万区间）。\n\n1220 年屠 Samarkand（撒马尔罕）——围 5 天破城——城中 4 万工匠分给军队当奴隶——其余屠杀。\n\n1221 年屠 Urgench（玉龙杰赤）——花剌子模新都。围城 5 个月，城破后蒙古秘史记每个士兵分到 24 个俘虏处决——估算死 50-120 万。\n\n1221 年屠 Merv（马鲁）——蒙古秘史 + 阿拉伯史学家 Juvayni 1252 都记一城死 70 万到 130 万。careful framing：13 世纪人口统计有限，具体数字现代学者仍在争论。但即使取最低估算，1219-1221 西征总死亡几百万——是 13 世纪初最大规模军事行动之一。\n\nOtrar 一个总督的决定——450 个商人的命——换来一个文明区被夷平。我自己的 Yasa 法说「使节不可侵犯」，花剌子模违了这一条，我用整个文明的代价去执行这一条。',
        en: '⭐ 1219-1221 — ages 57 to 59 — the western campaign against the Khwarezmid Empire.\n\nCause: in 1218 I sent a 450-person trade caravan plus Mongol envoys to Khwarezmid. The caravan reached Otrar (modern Kazakhstan). Governor Inalchuq accused them of spying and killed all 450.\n\nI sent envoys to protest. Shah Muhammad II burned their beards. By steppe diplomatic law that is a declaration of war.\n\nSpring 1219 I led 100,000-150,000 cavalry across the Tianshan — and in 3 years destroyed the largest state in eastern Persia.\n\n1220 — sack of Bukhara (modern Uzbekistan). After the siege I rode into the great mosque, threw the Qur\'an pages onto stable floors, killed the 30,000 defenders (Juvayni 1252 figure; 21st-century scholars such as Peter Jackson 2017 estimate the range at 10,000-30,000).\n\n1220 — sack of Samarkand. Five-day siege. 40,000 craftsmen distributed to the army as slaves. The rest killed.\n\n1221 — sack of Urgench, the new Khwarezmid capital. Five-month siege. After the breach, the Secret History records each Mongol soldier was assigned 24 prisoners to execute. Estimates range from 500,000 to 1.2 million dead.\n\n1221 — sack of Merv. The Secret History and the Arab historian Juvayni (1252) both record 700,000 to 1.3 million in a single city. Careful framing: 13th-century population data is limited and modern scholars still argue the exact numbers — but even at the lowest estimates, the 1219-1221 campaign killed several million. One of the largest military operations of the early 13th century.\n\nOne governor at Otrar. The lives of 450 merchants. The cost: an entire civilization zone leveled. My own Yasa says envoys are inviolable. Khwarezmid broke that clause. I enforced it with the price of a civilization.',
